  },
  "scenery": {
    "_doc": "Watercolour scenery for the Wash theme (asset packs). html[data-scenery] selects one on the web (classic, the default, sets nothing; localStorage mucli-scenery); Android stores @mucli/scenery. Classic keeps each destination's own scene and accent (destination). A pack paints every destination with its scene (<pack>-<theme> for the shell, ambient-<pack>-<theme> elsewhere, spot-<pack>-<theme> for plain empty states) and recolours every destination's accent to its pigment. Each pack is also listed in glass.ambient so its art is generated and contrast-checked. Flat palettes ignore scenery. leaf_clear (optional, 0–1) scales how much of the painting the glass leaf lets through, for paintings with darker passages: scripts/design/check_contrast.py applies the same factor. pages lists the destinations a pack painted on their own (wash/art/pages/<pack>/<page>-<theme> for the shell, pages/<pack>/ambient-<page>-<theme> elsewhere; Android assets/wash/pages/<pack>/): those destinations use their page art, the rest the pack's general scene. Page art is contrast-checked too.",
    "classic": {
      "label": "Classic",
